ck.md:216:without a `LineNumberTable`, so every dynamic-access frame is line-less\ndocs/metadata.md:29:  `resources`, `bundles`, `serialization`, and `foreignCalls` entries in the\ndocs/metadata.md:32:  `resource-config.json`, `serialization-config.json`, `proxy-config.json`) are\ndocs/grund.md:6:a shared, curated metadata source that fills the dynamic-access registrations\ndocs/goals.md:4:test that exhibits the dynamic access the metadata registers. Metadata is never\ndocs/goals.md:35:state of shipped metadata and its dynamic-access coverage, so additions never\ndocs/functional-spec.md:14:Reachability metadata describes reflection, JNI, resource access, serialization, and proxy use that GraalVM `native-image` cannot determine through static analysis. By centralizing this metadata, the repository allows libraries that are not yet self-contained for native compilation to \"just work\" with `native-image` when consumed via the GraalVM Gradle and Maven plugins.\ndocs/functional-spec.md:23:| **Repository automation (Forge)** | Generate or repair metadata using LLM-driven pipelines. | Per coordinate, the toolkit can: (1) **add support for a new library** — generate a JUnit / Kotlin / Scala test suite, scaffold metadata, and iterate until JVM-mode tests pass and dynamic-access is collected ([`add_new_library_support.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/add_new_library_support.py)); (2) **fix a Java compilation (`javac`) failure** raised by a library version bump ([`fix_javac_fail.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_javac_fail.py)); (3) **fix a JVM-mode (`javaTest`) runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_java_run_fail.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_java_run_fail.py)); (4) **fix a `native-image` runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_ni_run.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_ni_run.py)); (5) **improve dynamic-access coverage** of already-supported libraries by targeting uncovered call sites; (6) **post-generation repair** of the metadata produced by a previous run ([`fix_post_generation_pi.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/core/fix_post_generation_pi.py), [`fix_metadata_codex.py`](../forge/ai_workflows/core/fix_metadata_codex.py)). Each task runs Gradle tasks against a worktree of this repo, appends a schema-validated metrics record, and — when invoked through [`forge/git_scripts/make_pr_*.py`](../forge/git_scripts/) — opens a PR for human review. See [forge/docs/functional-spec.md](../forge/docs/functional-spec.md). |\ndocs/functional-spec.md:47:- A `stats/<groupId>/<artifactId>/<metadata-version>/` mirror of per-version metrics — `stats.json` (dynamic-access call sites, coverage, lines of code, dependency information) produced by the harness, alongside the schema-validated `execution-metrics.json` each Forge run records.\ndocs/functional-spec.md:59:- Coverage collection (JaCoCo) and dynamic-access reporting per coordinate.\ndocs/functional-spec.md:82:- `latest/badges.json` — badges shown in the README (libraries supported, tested versions, dynamic-access coverage, tested LOC).\ndocs/functional-spec.md:85:  `metadata/<group>/<artifact>/index.json` file and the dynamic-access coverage\ndocs/functional-spec.md:99:1. **Add new library support** — generate a JUnit test suite, scaffold metadata, iterate until JVM-mode tests pass and dynamic-access metadata is collected.\ndocs/functional-spec.md:102:4. **Improve coverage** of already-supported libraries by targeting uncovered dynamic-access call sites.\ndocs/functional-spec.md:129:| `chunked-dynamic-access` | Issue | Forge split dynamic-access generation for this issue into class-aligned chunks because the uncovered class count exceeded the configured threshold. Normal project status controls whether Forge may claim the next chunk. |\ndocs/functional-spec.md:155:    NI-->>App: native image with reflection / JNI /<br/>resources / serialization / proxies registered\ndocs/functional-spec.md:183:**3. `<groupId>/<artifactId>/<metadata-version>/reachability-metadata.json`** — the only file the plugin loads at native-image time. Schema [reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json](../metadata/schemas/reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json) (a vendored copy of the upstream GraalVM schema), with top-level keys `reflection`, `jni`, `resources`, `bundles`, `serialization`, and `foreignCalls`. Every entry's `condition` carries exactly one key, `typeReached`, so the plugin can rely on conditional registration; `typeReached` is the schema's only condition form. The legacy split-config layout (`reflect-config.json`, `jni-config.json`, …) is no longer present.\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:41:2. **Coverage improvement** — increase dynamic-access coverage of\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:45:   ordinary API and execution coverage beyond dynamic-access call coverage, as\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:78:code coverage, not only dynamic-access coverage (see\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:88:dynamic-access coverage workflow defined in §WF-improve-library-coverage.\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:100:| **Reachability metadata** | JSON describing reflection, JNI, resource, serialization, and proxy access for a library, consumed by GraalVM `native-image`. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:106:| **Workflow engine** | A registered state-machine-like workflow implementation among the core workflow objects in [ai_workflows/core/](../ai_workflows/core/), such as `basic_iterative` or `dynamic_access_iterative`. The engine owns prompts, command execution, retries, transitions, and terminal status selection for one run. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:110:| **Dynamic access** | Reflection, JNI, resource access, serialization, or proxy use that GraalVM `native-image` cannot determine statically. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:111:| **Dynamic-access report** | JSON written by Gradle task `generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport` to `tests/src/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/build/reports/dynamic-access/dynamic-access-coverage.json`, listing classes and per-class call sites that require dynamic-access metadata, marked covered/uncovered. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:112:| **Dynamic-access exhaust report** | Durable coordinate-scoped JSON state for chunked dynamic-access work. It records the coordinate, issue number, class threshold, completed/skipped/exhausted/failed classes, and the latest published chunk PR/commit. It is stored in a stable location derived from the target test suite (for example under `tests/src/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/`) so orchestration scripts can find it from the coordinate alone. It does not predefine all chunks; each resume regenerates the current dynamic-access report and filters out processed classes. Specified by §WF-dynamic-access-exhaust-report. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:113:| **Chunked dynamic-access workflow** | Dynamic-access generation mode for oversized `library-new-request` issues and `library-update-request` issues routed to dynamic-access coverage improvement. `forge_metadata.py` owns the class threshold decision and passes the current chunk size to the workflow. The workflow processes at most that many uncovered classes, publishes that chunk, then resumes after the chunk PR merges. PR linking rules are in §WF-chunked-dynamic-access-pr-linking. |\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:144:- `--keep-tests-without-dynamic-access` — only honored by dynamic-access\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:145:  workflows (§WF-dynamic-access-workflow).\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:174:  `library-update-request` issues routed to dynamic-access coverage improvement,\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:178:  If the current dynamic-access report has more uncovered classes than this\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:199:  testing, dynamic-access reporting, native metadata exploration, metadata\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:483:zero dynamic-access calls are never human-intervention on their own, because the\nforge/docs/functional-spec.md:486:(§FS-zero-dynamic-access-tolerance).\nforge/docs/functional-spec.